WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.000
Let’s walk through Exports.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.362
An export is evidence tied to one selected session.

00:00:05.362 --> 00:00:08.537
Reconcile the session identity and run state first, choose

00:00:08.537 --> 00:00:10.925
the format for the intended review, and retain the

00:00:10.925 --> 00:00:13.988
manifest that explains what the archive contains.

00:00:13.988 --> 00:00:17.300
On this slide, produce JSON, CSV, or

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.688
research archives from the explicitly selected session.

00:00:20.688 --> 00:00:24.550
In practice, export only after reconciling session identity and

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:25.650
run state.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.762
The archive is evidence, not a control action.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:32.060
When you are ready, use Open Exports to move

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:33.547
to the live surface.

00:00:33.547 --> 00:00:36.260
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:36.410
.
